  "Renouf and Naville 1904 opened at the cited Project Gutenberg transcription; each cited reading found verbatim: walls of steel; wheat seven, ears two, stalks five; glorified ones seven cubits then nine; sycamores of emerald; three hundred measures in length and ten in width; seventy cubits in his windings; thighs of seven cubits; backbone seven cubits; four snakes; fifteen domains instead of fourteen, the fifth divided; I adopt Renouf's translation; only four yellow, 3, 9, 10 and 14; near the stream of the lake; islands of the wandering stars; drives the Nile towards Tattu; two wells at Elephantine.",
